  "generated_text": "1. The centers of the circles are \\((2,0)\\) and \\((5,0)\\).\n2. The line is tangent to both circles in the first quadrant.\n3. The radii of the circles are 2 and 1, respectively.\n4. The distance between the centers of the circles is \\(5 - 2 = 3\\).\n5. The line is tangent to both circles, so it must be perpendicular to the line connecting the centers.\n6. The slope of the line connecting the centers is \\(\\frac{0 - 0}{5 - 2} = 0\\).\n7. Since the tangent line is perpendicular to the line connecting the centers, its slope is the negative reciprocal of \\(0\\), which is \\(\\text{undefined}\\).\n8. A vertical line has an undefined slope.\n9. Therefore, the tangent line must be vertical.\n10. A vertical line passing through the point \\((2,0)\\) has a \\(y\\)-intercept of \\(0\\).\n\nThus, the \\(y\\)-intercept of the line tangent to both circles in the first quadrant is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{0}\n\\]",
